NNAAMMEE
     yyppppuusshh — force distribution of one YP map

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     yyppppuusshh [--vv] [--dd _d_o_m_a_i_n_n_a_m_e] [--hh _h_o_s_t_n_a_m_e] _m_a_p_n_a_m_e

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The yyppppuusshh utility distributes one YP map from the master server to all
     slave servers in the domain.  All servers of the domain are fetched from
     the YP map _y_p_s_e_r_v_e_r_s.  Before starting distribution, the master server is
     told to reread its Berkeley DB map files from disk.

     The options are as follows:

     --dd _d_o_m_a_i_n_n_a_m_e
             Don't use the default domain, use the specified domain.

     --hh _h_o_s_t_n_a_m_e
             Distribute the map only to one host and not to the hosts in the
             _y_p_s_e_r_v_e_r_s map.

     --vv      Verbose.  Announce what the program is doing.

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     dbopen(3), Makefile.yp(8), yp(8), ypserv(8)

